{"book":"transformations","bookTitle":"Transformations, symmetry and position","concept":4,"title":"Coordinates in four quadrants","grades":"Grades 6–7","goal":"I can read and plot points in all four quadrants.","teach":"A point is written (x; y). From the origin, x tells you how far across (right is positive, left is negative) and y how far up or down (up is positive, down is negative). The axes make four <b>quadrants</b>, numbered anticlockwise from the top right: first (+; +), second (−; +), third (−; −), fourth (+; −). A point on an axis is in no quadrant.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:419px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 322 256\"><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"76\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"102\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"102\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"128\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"154\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"154\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"206\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"206\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"232\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"232\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"258\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"258\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"284\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"284\" y2=\"24\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"284\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"284\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"284\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"284\" y2=\"154\" stroke=\"#ddd\" stroke-wi